        "Takashi Mimura"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The high-electron-mobility transistor is a clear, consequential device invention that enabled major advances in high-frequency electronics and communications.",
        "attribution": "Mimura is credited as the inventor, making the contribution unusually focused and legible for a prize.",
        "maturity": "The device has had decades of validation and widespread technological impact.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The historical record should establish how the invention was shared with other researchers in the development team."
        ]
      }
    },
